usage_tracker: mark every 64-byte block a range touches (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 765659af4c (branch oot-gather-fix, v2), which carries zortos293's e8be5d3d59
(masks) and b16ba4f0dc (reset guard, ported from sylvieistaken/selevet-eglantine d8c95fef47).

EDEN_NX2_USAGE_EXACT=1. TrackPage and IsPageUsed count size >> 6 blocks from the first one. A range
that is not 64-byte aligned covers one block more than that, and the last one was never marked. A
range under 64 bytes gives 0 blocks and a shift by 64, undefined in C++. The answer decides
CanReorderUpload: a region read as unused lets an upload move ahead of the frame's draws, so a draw
could read the new data early. With the switch every touched block counts and empty ranges do
nothing. Also skips the per-frame clear for buffers nothing tracked since the last one.

Changed from the source: off by default, there always on. Reset stays as it was and the guard is a
new ResetIfTracked, so lichii-cpu-0235 still applies.

Runs on the PS5: same core path. Whether the console ever hits the bad order is unknown.
Hang: none, no wait added. More regions read as used, so a few uploads stop being reordered.
Pool memory: none. Two bools per buffer.
Checked: applies on core16, and in both orders with lichii-cpu-0234 and 0235. PS5-target syntax compile of
vk_buffer_cache.cpp, no errors. Real header against the old one and a byte model, 863,213 random
queries: switch off, 0 differences from the old header; switch on, 0 differences from the model. The
old code said unused where used 856 times of 271,310. IsUsed also checks from the page start when
the range ends on the same page, in core16 and in Lichii: harmless, says used more often, left alone.
Not run on the console.

Co-authored-by: zortos293 <65777760+zortos293@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/usage_tracker.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/usage_tracker.h
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/usage_tracker.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/usage_tracker.h
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <array>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 #include "common/alignment.h"
 #include "common/common_types.h"
@@ -24,8 +25,23 @@
     explicit UsageTracker(size_t size) {
         const size_t num_pages = (size >> BUFFER_PAGE_SHIFT) + 1;
         pages.resize(num_pages, 0ULL);
+        // EDEN_NX2_USAGE_EXACT=1: a function-local static, env.txt is read in main.
+        static const bool exact_blocks = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_USAGE_EXACT");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+        exact = exact_blocks;
     }
 
+    /// Reset, skipped with EDEN_NX2_USAGE_EXACT=1 for a tracker untouched since the last one.
+    void ResetIfTracked() noexcept {
+        if (exact && !tracked) {
+            return;
+        }
+        tracked = false;
+        Reset();
+    }
+
     void Reset() noexcept {
         std::ranges::fill(pages, 0ULL);
         recent.fill({~u64{0}, 0});
@@ -40,6 +56,7 @@
                 return;
             }
         }
+        tracked = true;
         recent[recent_cursor++ % recent.size()] = {offset, size};
         const size_t page = offset >> BUFFER_PAGE_SHIFT;
         const size_t page_end = (offset + size) >> BUFFER_PAGE_SHIFT;
@@ -81,7 +98,11 @@
     void TrackPage(u64 page, u64 offset, u64 size) noexcept {
         const size_t offset_in_page = offset % BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES;
         const size_t first_bit = offset_in_page >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
-        const size_t num_bits = std::min<size_t>(size, BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES) >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
+        if (exact && size == 0) {
+            return;
+        }
+        const size_t num_bits = exact ? ExactBits(offset_in_page, size)
+                                      : std::min<size_t>(size, BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES) >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
         const size_t mask = ~u64{0} >> (64 - num_bits);
         pages[page] |= (~u64{0} & mask) << first_bit;
     }
@@ -89,13 +110,26 @@
     bool IsPageUsed(u64 page, u64 offset, u64 size) const noexcept {
         const size_t offset_in_page = offset % BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES;
         const size_t first_bit = offset_in_page >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
-        const size_t num_bits = std::min<size_t>(size, BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES) >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
+        if (exact && size == 0) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        const size_t num_bits = exact ? ExactBits(offset_in_page, size)
+                                      : std::min<size_t>(size, BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES) >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
         const size_t mask = ~u64{0} >> (64 - num_bits);
         const size_t mask2 = (~u64{0} & mask) << first_bit;
         return (pages[page] & mask2) != 0;
     }
 
+    /// Blocks from the first one that a range of size bytes at offset_in_page touches.
+    size_t ExactBits(size_t offset_in_page, u64 size) const noexcept {
+        const size_t bytes = std::min<size_t>(size, BUFFER_PAGE_BYTES - offset_in_page);
+        const size_t last_bit = (offset_in_page + bytes - 1) >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT;
+        return last_bit - (offset_in_page >> BUFFER_BYTES_PER_BITSHIFT) + 1;
+    }
+
 private:
+    bool exact{};
+    bool tracked{};
     std::vector<u64> pages;
     /// Ranges tracked last, (offset, size).
     std::array<std::pair<u64, u64>, 4> recent{{{~u64{0}, 0}, {~u64{0}, 0}, {~u64{0}, 0}, {~u64{0}, 0}}};
